; The in-server console EVAL ENGINE — a dev-only, bytecode-only library that hosts the OCaml toplevel
; INSIDE the running app server, so a REPL evaluates against the server's OWN linked modules and LIVE
; state (the open burrow, booted Accounts, in-flight fibers) — the `iex -S mix phx.server` model.
;
; It links [compiler-libs.toplevel], so it must NEVER reach the prod binary; it is byte-only (the
; toplevel is bytecode) and registers itself through the dev hook ([Fennec.set_console_hook]) rather
; than being referenced by fennec's core. The dev server build links it with -linkall (so the toplevel
; can resolve every linked module); the prod native build links neither it nor the compiler.
(library
 (name console_engine)
 (public_name fennec.console.engine)
 (modes byte)
 (libraries
  fennec
  fennec.console.protocol
  compiler-libs.toplevel
  eio
  eio.unix
  unix
  fennec-hunt.unit)
 (inline_tests
  (backend fennec-hunt.runner))
 (preprocess
  (pps fennec-hunt.ppx)))
